content.reasoning:
Same generic error.

Wait, earlier I got a different error for zone-2c19 + combined + 12 + 30: "field": "zone_id" error. Let me see what was different there.

Earlier I sent: {zone_id: "zone-2c19", phase: "combined", flowRateLpm: 12, duration: {value: 30, unit: "minutes"}}
And got: {"error": "missing_required", "field": "zone_id", "hint": "zone_id is required; fetch a zone_id from GET /v3/zones"}

Now I sent: {zone_id: "zone-2c19", phase: "combined", flowRateLpm: 8, duration: {value: 45, unit: "minutes"}}
And got: generic error with all fields.

The difference is the flowRateLpm and duration values. So the server's response depends on the values. Maybe when zone-2c19 + combined + 12 + 30, the server thinks zone_id is missing (because it's a specific reserved combination?). When the values are different, it gives a generic error.

This is very inconsistent. It suggests the server has a complex or buggy validation.

Let me try zone-2c19 + combined + 12 + 30 again to confirm the zone_id error.
